 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nColumn qualification fails for multi-part column references\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen qualifying columns in SQL queries, multi-part column references (like `table.column` or `schema.table.column`) are not being properly handled, causing qualification to fail silently and leaving columns unqualified.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot import optimizer\n\n# This should qualify the column reference but doesn't\nquery = sqlglot.parse_one('select a.b:c from d', read='snowflake')\nqualified = optimizer.qualify.qualify(query)\nprint(f\"Expected alias: 'c', Got: {qualified.expressions[0].alias}\")\n\n# Another example with multi-part references\nquery2 = sqlglot.parse_one('SELECT Teams.Name FROM raw.Teams')\nqualified2 = optimizer.qualify_columns.qualify_columns(query2, schema={'raw': {'Teams': {'Name': 'STRING'}}})\nprint(qualified2.sql())\n```\n\nThe column qualification process should properly handle multi-part column references by resolving the table name and qualifying the column accordingly. Currently, these references are being skipped during the qualification process.\n</issue>\n",
